{"kind":"stack","id":"stack-flowers","title":"How flowers make seeds","theme":{"background":"#f4fbf2","foreground":"#1d3b1a","font":"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Pollination"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"When pollen moves from the anther of one flower to the stigma of a flower. Insects, wind and water can carry the pollen."}],"actions":[],"buttons":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1b","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1b-t","content":"Seed dispersal"},{"type":"text","id":"c1b-e","content":"How seeds travel away from the parent plant. Seeds can be carried by wind, water, animals or by bursting out of the fruit."}],"actions":[],"buttons":[]}}
